<title>INDIA: India soybean, meal steady, oil firm.</title>
<headline>India soybean, meal steady, oil firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets in very thin trading as arrivals were poor on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 1,000 tonnes in central Indian markets, as compared to around 15,000 tonnes per day at the same time last year.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained firm on limited supply against good demand in local markets. Soyoil prices rose by 200 rupees per tonne. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady. Soymeal yellow was $320-321 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $123-124 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export and was 4,250-4,300 rupees FOR (Free On Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
